WEBVTT

00:04.290 --> 00:07.000
Alrighty, Max! Sorry for the wait.

00:07.000 --> 00:09.540
I made your favorite, Hamburg steak!

00:08.790 --> 00:12.420
<b>Superstar of the Day</b>

00:09.540 --> 00:12.420
Was all this really necessary? Jeez...

00:12.580 --> 00:13.960
Hey, you jerk!

00:13.960 --> 00:15.670
Don't get started without me!

00:15.670 --> 00:17.580
We're supposed to raise a toast together.

00:17.580 --> 00:19.580
What, with non-alcoholic cider?

00:19.580 --> 00:21.540
Oh, just open it already.

00:22.330 --> 00:24.250
Crap, crap, crap!

00:24.580 --> 00:24.830
Whoa, look at it go!
It's gettin' everywhere!<b></b>

00:24.830 --> 00:26.290
Tsk...
Whoa, look at it go!<b>
It's gettin' everywhere!</b>

00:26.670 --> 00:28.500
Do somethin', wouldja?!

00:29.420 --> 00:36.250
<b>#12 The Fruits of Their Labor</b>

00:31.580 --> 00:33.290
What's the matter, Max?

00:33.290 --> 00:35.170
You stopped eating...

00:35.170 --> 00:36.920
Was it not to your liking?

00:36.920 --> 00:39.670
N-no... Ya made way too much...

00:39.670 --> 00:41.580
How many people does this feed?

00:41.580 --> 00:43.040
I feel a food coma coming on...

00:43.580 --> 00:47.420
I don't know how ya managed to make
all this in my tiny kitchen...

00:47.420 --> 00:50.500
Even the pizza and the cake
are made from scratch...

00:50.500 --> 00:53.380
And yet you've barely even made a dent in it!

00:53.380 --> 00:56.830
It's not every day we get to celebrate
the Hero and his victories, y'know.

00:58.500 --> 01:02.880
This squishy little potbelly of yours
doesn't even fit in your pants, does it?

01:03.170 --> 01:04.330
Knock it off...

01:05.290 --> 01:07.500
But it seems like you can
move around just fine.

01:07.830 --> 01:08.710
You jiggle like jelly.

01:08.710 --> 01:09.540
Jiggle?!

01:09.790 --> 01:11.540
No, I do NOT jiggle!

01:11.540 --> 01:12.630
...or do I?

01:12.630 --> 01:13.540
Well...

01:13.540 --> 01:15.580
Hm, I dunno!

01:15.580 --> 01:16.540
I don't, right?

01:16.540 --> 01:17.710
I could strangle him...

01:17.710 --> 01:18.630
RIGHT?!
I could strangle him...<b></b>

01:19.920 --> 01:20.880
Jiggle...

01:23.920 --> 01:25.880
You were amazing, Max.

01:26.250 --> 01:29.380
Not only did you defeat Leo and Fred...

01:29.380 --> 01:31.210
You saved them, too.

01:31.790 --> 01:35.250
Plus, you ensured a future for
the Kingdom and the Republic.

01:35.580 --> 01:38.420
It's not like I did it all on my own.

01:38.420 --> 01:41.420
If it weren't for Yuria, I would've died.

01:41.790 --> 01:43.420
She's the one to thank.

01:44.170 --> 01:45.880
And you, for that matter.

01:47.750 --> 01:50.330
Oh, but I didn't... really do anything...

01:50.630 --> 01:52.380
That ain't true at all.

01:52.380 --> 01:54.080
Yes, it is...

01:58.130 --> 01:59.540
Thanks.

02:02.380 --> 02:05.210
You're right, I made a little too much.

02:05.210 --> 02:07.460
We'll just have to eat
the leftovers tomorrow.

02:07.460 --> 02:09.170
Guess so.

02:09.170 --> 02:11.420
I'm stuffed, so now I'm gettin' sleepy.

02:11.420 --> 02:13.920
I'm sure we can finish it off
if I invite Zenia.

02:13.920 --> 02:16.670
Then why not just have her come over now?

02:16.670 --> 02:19.540
Seriously? It's not THAT important.

02:19.790 --> 02:20.790
Tsk...

02:22.790 --> 02:24.420
YOUR GRACE!

02:24.420 --> 02:27.040
FORGIVE ME, I BEG OF YOU!

02:27.040 --> 02:27.920
PLEASE! PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE!

02:27.920 --> 02:30.250
What in the devil is going on, Zenia?
PLEASE! PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE!<b></b>

02:30.540 --> 02:33.580
Well... I was using my personal laptop

02:33.580 --> 02:36.710
to analyze the data on the computer
I swiped from the Magic Bureau, when...

02:38.250 --> 02:41.460
There's all sorts of data on here,
but I'm not sure what it means...

02:42.330 --> 02:43.920
Huh? What's this?

02:43.920 --> 02:47.920
<b>Click here for a fun surprise</b>

02:44.330 --> 02:46.880
"Click here for a fun surprise"...?

02:46.880 --> 02:47.920
And... click!

02:47.920 --> 02:49.830
<b>All of your data has been stolen :(</b>

02:48.290 --> 02:49.830
WHAT?!

02:50.170 --> 02:52.500
In other words, it was a computer virus, eh?

02:52.500 --> 02:54.500
Oh well, what's done is done.

02:54.500 --> 02:56.290
Honestly, I totally forgot about that...

02:56.290 --> 02:58.710
Thank you for forgiving me, milord!

03:00.460 --> 03:02.750
What's this all about?

03:02.750 --> 03:04.960
Oh, is it your birthday, Max?

03:04.960 --> 03:05.670
Huh?!

03:05.670 --> 03:08.920
Oh, that's right.
You have no idea, do you?

03:08.920 --> 03:09.580
You should see it.

03:09.580 --> 03:10.130
That's not necessary!
You should see it.<b></b>

03:10.130 --> 03:11.000
That's not necessary!

03:11.000 --> 03:13.670
And coming up next:
The story behind this viral video.

03:13.670 --> 03:17.830
There HAS to be a way for us
to settle this without violence!

03:18.210 --> 03:21.580
The video was streamed live
online a few days ago;

03:21.580 --> 03:36.290
<b>NEW      Beskar Kingdom</b>

03:21.580 --> 03:36.290
<b>The Country's Stance on the Republic has Changed Drastically</b>

03:21.590 --> 03:26.290
since then, relations between the Kingdom
and the Republic have changed drastically.

03:26.710 --> 03:29.580
In response to a shift in public opinion,

03:29.580 --> 03:32.210
the royal government softened
its stance on the Republic

03:32.210 --> 03:36.290
and ultimately chose to recognize
its status as an autonomous territory.

03:36.290 --> 03:42.000
<b>What does the future hold for</b>

03:36.290 --> 03:42.000
<b>the Kingdom and the Republic?</b>

03:36.290 --> 03:42.000
<b>Man, 20s</b>

03:36.750 --> 03:38.420
Came as a surprise to me.

03:38.420 --> 03:42.000
But I'm glad they managed to
work it out peacefully, y'know?

03:42.000 --> 03:44.920
The Hero's insanely strong!

03:42.000 --> 03:49.210
<b>What does the future hold for</b>

03:42.000 --> 03:49.210
<b>the Kingdom and the Republic?</b>

03:42.000 --> 03:49.210
<b>Woman, 20s</b>

03:42.000 --> 03:49.210
<b>Man, 30s</b>

03:44.920 --> 03:46.330
He was awesome!

03:46.330 --> 03:49.210
It was so cool! Even the whole groveling part!

03:49.500 --> 03:51.750
Wow, that's fantastic, Max!

03:51.750 --> 03:53.670
You're awfully popular, aren't you?

03:53.670 --> 03:55.710
You did a great job!

04:08.330 --> 04:10.000
So fast...

04:10.250 --> 04:12.500
I'm beginning to see how
a handful of people

04:12.500 --> 04:15.290
managed to build a city
and a fortress so quickly...

04:15.290 --> 04:16.750
Here, have some tea.

04:18.380 --> 04:20.580
Our boss is impressive, isn't he?

04:20.580 --> 04:23.630
Us Kingdom guys really appreciate
your hospitality.

04:23.630 --> 04:25.250
Oh, don't be silly!

04:25.250 --> 04:28.000
There's no "Kingdom" or "Republic"
anymore, right?

04:28.000 --> 04:31.630
Since we're an autonomous territory
of the Kingdom now.

04:31.790 --> 04:34.830
But... are you okay with that?

04:34.830 --> 04:36.960
I thought you wanted independence...

04:36.960 --> 04:39.750
Nah... For us and the boss,

04:39.750 --> 04:43.670
our goal was never something as big or
as flashy as having our own country.

04:43.670 --> 04:48.000
All we wanted was to protect the land
we'd worked hard to develop.

04:48.290 --> 04:51.630
This whole debacle started because
the Kingdom decided to

04:51.630 --> 04:54.500
try and kick us out and seize it from us.

04:54.500 --> 04:58.250
Boy, am I relieved that we finally
came to a compromise!

04:58.830 --> 05:00.750
Things really worked out for the best.

05:00.750 --> 05:04.960
And now we get to build a road together,
one that connects us to the Kingdom.

05:05.420 --> 05:08.040
I bet you'll get plenty of tourists, too.

05:08.040 --> 05:09.420
International and domestic.

05:09.420 --> 05:11.750
Our hot springs are our specialty.

05:11.750 --> 05:15.880
Through the power of magic ore,
they'll leave your skin feeling silky smooth!

05:15.880 --> 05:18.170
Stop by and try 'em after work sometime.

05:18.170 --> 05:21.290
Oh, this rocks!

05:26.830 --> 05:28.960
It's comin' along nicely...

05:28.960 --> 05:30.790
Just a little more till I reach the town.

05:30.790 --> 05:32.420
Hey, Boss!

05:34.130 --> 05:37.290
Whoops... Am I supposed to
call you "Mr. Mayor" now?

05:37.290 --> 05:39.130
Oh please, spare me.

05:39.130 --> 05:41.250
A title like that doesn't suit me at all.

05:41.420 --> 05:45.080
You're working awfully fast for someone
who suffered severe injuries.

05:45.080 --> 05:47.210
Didn't you have a gaping hole in your chest?

05:47.210 --> 05:49.380
Ah, that was just a flesh wound!

05:50.250 --> 05:51.420
That's a lie!

05:51.420 --> 05:53.960
For a while there, you couldn't even move!

05:53.960 --> 05:55.960
I swear, he's indestructible...

05:56.170 --> 06:01.210
Still, the battle reminded me of just how
incredible the Hero and his pals are.

06:01.210 --> 06:04.920
The Kingdom's lucky Max
showed up when he did.

06:04.920 --> 06:05.710
Hm?

06:05.710 --> 06:09.250
Had you and Fred fought one-on-one,
you definitely would've won, Boss.

06:09.250 --> 06:10.460
Don'tcha think?

06:10.830 --> 06:12.380
Who knows?

06:12.670 --> 06:15.670
Either way, it wouldn't have done any good.

06:16.040 --> 06:20.330
THEY'RE the reason we were able to mend
our relationship with the Kingdom.

06:20.330 --> 06:22.750
And that's not something I could've done.

06:25.130 --> 06:28.540
He really is amazing, isn't he?
The Hero...

06:29.130 --> 06:33.130
C'mon! Out with the Gamma Republic,
in with Gamma Province!

06:33.130 --> 06:35.210
We've still got tons of stuff to get done!

06:35.210 --> 06:36.330
Let's go!

06:36.330 --> 06:37.500
Yeah!

06:41.790 --> 06:46.080
There HAS to be a way for us
to settle this without violence!

06:46.460 --> 06:48.960
Another news story about Max?

06:48.960 --> 06:51.170
How many times are they
going to play this video...?

06:51.540 --> 06:53.790
The public is well aware, sir.

06:53.790 --> 06:56.500
They know you were the one
who put his life on the line

06:56.500 --> 06:58.380
and fought for the good of the Kingdom.

06:59.630 --> 07:02.880
Chief Secretary, how have you
been feeling lately?

07:02.880 --> 07:06.460
If you intend to take some time off,
then I have something for you.

07:06.460 --> 07:10.080
I happened across some exceedingly
valuable data the other day.

07:10.080 --> 07:12.630
What? What "valuable data"?

07:15.290 --> 07:16.330
What?!

07:17.330 --> 07:18.130
<b>Burn</b>

07:18.580 --> 07:20.580
If you'll excuse me, I'll be going now.

07:32.960 --> 07:35.540
Hello, everybody! My name's Macky!

07:35.540 --> 07:38.880
Please be sure to like,
comment, and subscribe!

07:38.880 --> 07:42.380
So today, I'm going to drop
this candy into this soda...

07:42.380 --> 07:44.420
Both the video quality and
the sound quality suck ass...
...and then we'll see if it explodes!<b></b>

07:44.420 --> 07:45.540
Both the video quality and
the sound quality suck ass...
Okay, Mr. Soda...<b></b>

07:45.540 --> 07:46.880
The content is stale, unoriginal,
and disorganized...

07:46.880 --> 07:48.580
The content is stale, unoriginal,
and disorganized...
Time to meet your doom!<b></b>

07:48.580 --> 07:50.080
And he rambles on forever...

07:52.500 --> 07:55.380
S-subscribe to my channel,
please and thank you!

07:56.040 --> 07:58.290
And why's he filming from so far away...?

07:58.290 --> 08:08.040
<b>Super Scrumptious Sweets</b>

07:58.290 --> 08:08.040
<b>Review</b>

07:59.670 --> 08:02.960
Oh man, I love me some sweets
from the convenience store!

08:02.960 --> 08:05.540
Remember, I'm always open to suggestions!

08:05.540 --> 08:08.040
You have no business
asking anyone for anything!

08:09.080 --> 08:11.290
Is, um, the camera rolling...?

08:13.290 --> 08:15.460
He even roped that woman into helping him...

08:15.460 --> 08:17.500
God, what a creep.

08:17.920 --> 08:19.080
Huh?

08:27.630 --> 08:29.630
Your face is so scary!

08:29.630 --> 08:30.960
Yeah, I know...

08:30.960 --> 08:33.290
Just learn from me!

08:33.580 --> 08:37.210
I mean, even today I went out of my way
to brighten the Chief Secretary's day

08:37.210 --> 08:39.830
after he got all jealous about Max!

08:39.830 --> 08:42.710
He must be over the moon right now.

08:42.710 --> 08:45.880
Thanks to that, you can bet that I'm gonna be
in his good graces from now on!

08:45.880 --> 08:47.960
Maybe in more ways than one!

08:47.960 --> 08:49.330
Shucks!

08:58.420 --> 09:01.380
Whaddya think you're doing?
Turn off the camera!

09:10.170 --> 09:12.000
Hmph! This doesn't sit right with me!

09:12.000 --> 09:14.290
To hell with the "Gamma Province"!

09:14.290 --> 09:15.960
It's a bunch of bullcrap!

09:15.960 --> 09:19.420
What else can we do?
It's the will of the people.

09:19.420 --> 09:21.000
Will of the people, my ass!

09:21.000 --> 09:24.580
All it took was one lousy livestream,

09:24.580 --> 09:28.330
and everybody suddenly hopped on the damn
sympathy train for the Hero and his party!

09:28.330 --> 09:31.420
They have no idea how cheaply
our magic ore resources got bought out

09:31.420 --> 09:34.420
by Trachigo and other countries
thanks to those fools!

09:34.420 --> 09:35.670
Oh, come on.

09:35.670 --> 09:37.920
You shouldn't be so greedy.

09:37.920 --> 09:38.920
Say what?!

09:40.330 --> 09:43.330
Well, it was an unfortunate
turn of events for you.

09:43.330 --> 09:45.540
But I must say,
I never imagined that rascal Max

09:45.540 --> 09:48.920
still had the guts to put
his life on the line like that.

09:48.920 --> 09:51.130
I'm seeing him in a bit of a new light.

09:51.130 --> 09:54.880
The people of the Kingdom also knew
the time to end the war was close at hand.

09:54.880 --> 09:58.750
And thankfully, Sir Max created the
perfect opportunity for that to happen.

09:58.920 --> 10:02.830
But ya know, I'm not sure it's wise to
give the providence any special treatment.

10:02.830 --> 10:05.750
They might let it go to their heads
and start defying us again.

10:05.750 --> 10:07.460
No, that shouldn't be a problem.

10:07.460 --> 10:10.250
Leo is the type of man who always
returns courtesy with courtesy.

10:10.250 --> 10:12.710
He's been that way ever since
he was in the military.

10:12.710 --> 10:14.960
Except he returns insolence
with insolence, too.

10:14.960 --> 10:17.170
That's how we got into this mess
in the first place.

10:17.170 --> 10:19.210
Enough. You need to shut your mouth.

10:19.210 --> 10:22.790
Everybody calm down.
Let's get back to the matter at hand.

10:22.790 --> 10:24.630
We don't want to just keep stirring the pot.

10:25.290 --> 10:27.630
Isn't that right, Chief Secretary Fred?

10:27.630 --> 10:30.130
That was a hell of a fight you put up.

10:30.130 --> 10:31.790
I was watching it, too.

10:32.000 --> 10:34.880
All right. Here's a question for you,
Chief Secretary.

10:34.880 --> 10:39.420
You were aware that your actions were
being recorded by a drone, right?

10:39.420 --> 10:40.250
Yes.

10:40.250 --> 10:43.630
Then why the blazes didn't you
destroy the drone immediately?!

10:43.630 --> 10:47.630
Oh. Well, that's because I thought
it was just a bird or something.

10:47.630 --> 10:49.290
W-why you sonnuva...!

10:49.710 --> 10:51.830
Okay, but even if we put that aside,

10:51.830 --> 10:55.170
you still used magic to attack
my subordinate, Colonel Gelmof,

10:55.170 --> 10:56.880
which left him severely injured.

10:56.880 --> 10:59.040
I can't let you off the hook for that.

10:59.040 --> 11:02.540
Fair enough, but considering that he
went on to fight against both Max and Leo,

11:02.540 --> 11:05.170
his efforts directly contributed to
the peaceful resolutio-

11:05.170 --> 11:06.000
No!

11:06.000 --> 11:08.710
Max could easily have done that
all by himself!

11:08.710 --> 11:10.500
You big oaf.

11:10.500 --> 11:15.250
Max never would have shown up if Leo
and Fred hadn't started fighting each other.

11:15.250 --> 11:18.920
Everyone in the Hero's party
deserves credit for the end result.

11:18.920 --> 11:20.920
Am I right, Fred?

11:21.080 --> 11:23.000
From the moment I attacked the colonel,

11:23.000 --> 11:26.130
I've been prepared to face whatever
punishment was deemed fit.

11:26.420 --> 11:29.040
And just as the honorable
Second Minister said,

11:29.040 --> 11:32.880
I don't believe I deserve any credit
for how things turned out.

11:32.880 --> 11:35.960
Then you're going to have to resign from
your position as Chief Secretary.

11:35.960 --> 11:37.830
Yes, that's fine with me.

11:37.830 --> 11:41.040
However, that doesn't put everything to rest.

11:41.040 --> 11:43.750
We still need to sort out the
explosive "accident" that occurred

11:43.750 --> 11:45.250
at the Magic Bureau the other day.

11:46.630 --> 11:47.670
Gosh!

11:47.670 --> 11:51.920
You know, I was totally convinced it was
a terrorist attack by the Gamma Republic!

11:51.920 --> 11:55.460
I never would have guessed that it was just
a magical experiment gone wrong.

11:55.460 --> 11:58.080
This is nothing to laugh about,
Minister Grimms!

11:58.080 --> 12:00.670
Because I firmly came down
against the terrorists

12:00.670 --> 12:02.920
when I spoke to the media
about it afterwards!

12:02.920 --> 12:04.790
From the Republic's perspective,

12:04.790 --> 12:07.710
it must seem like were trying to
pin the blame on them.

12:07.880 --> 12:10.380
But Leo was kind enough
to overlook the whole thing.

12:10.380 --> 12:14.170
So as far as we're concerned,
he actually saved us from quite a mess.

12:14.170 --> 12:16.830
We might as well hear what
you have to say, Fred.

12:16.830 --> 12:18.630
How did this accident happen?

12:18.630 --> 12:21.130
Surely you must have some idea.

12:21.130 --> 12:23.420
I'm afraid that I have no idea
what you're referring to.

12:23.670 --> 12:24.920
It's simple, really.

12:24.920 --> 12:29.790
I had previously heard from Grimms that you
were in an absolutely foul mood as of late.

12:29.790 --> 12:32.790
And since a confrontation with
your former allies was brewing,

12:32.790 --> 12:36.130
it stands to reason that you would want
something to act as a catalyst

12:36.130 --> 12:37.540
to get it over with quickly.

12:38.750 --> 12:40.750
Huh? What?!

12:43.920 --> 12:45.290
I see.

12:45.290 --> 12:47.130
Since I'm already on the chopping block,

12:47.130 --> 12:49.130
you want to make me the scapegoat
for all your inconvenient problems.

12:49.130 --> 12:51.250
How big brained of you.

12:51.460 --> 12:52.790
Then go right ahead.

12:52.790 --> 12:54.880
You're so hasty, I swear.

13:10.630 --> 13:12.290
Huh? What's the deal?

13:12.290 --> 13:13.580
Is something wrong?

13:13.580 --> 13:16.170
Third Minister Grimms.

13:16.170 --> 13:18.290
We have a warrant for your arrest.

13:18.290 --> 13:19.420
HUH?!

13:19.750 --> 13:20.880
WHAT?!

13:20.880 --> 13:23.670
Whoa, no way! H-hold the phone!

13:23.670 --> 13:24.790
Why me?!

13:24.790 --> 13:28.080
I mean, we just figured out Fred was
responsible for the explosion!

13:28.080 --> 13:30.460
Me? Really? That makes no sense!

13:30.460 --> 13:33.380
I didn't do jack shit! Show me the proof!

13:33.380 --> 13:34.920
You can't pin the explosion on me!

13:35.130 --> 13:37.330
I'm not sure why you would bring that up.

13:37.330 --> 13:40.170
Because you're wanted for the crime
of embezzling public funds.

13:40.920 --> 13:42.130
Come again?!

13:42.290 --> 13:45.460
There is an unknown source that has
been randomly sending out data

13:45.460 --> 13:48.040
to email addresses across the world,

13:48.040 --> 13:52.290
and included among it was detailed financial
data for the Kingdom's Magic Bureau.

13:48.040 --> 13:52.290
<b>LEDGER</b>

13:52.920 --> 13:55.830
Examination of that information revealed
that part of bureau's budget

13:52.920 --> 13:56.380
<b>Withdrawals</b>

13:52.920 --> 13:56.380
<b>Deposits</b>

13:55.830 --> 13:57.960
was being passed through
a dummy account,

13:57.960 --> 14:02.210
and then later deposited into a
bank account belonging to you, sir.

14:02.750 --> 14:05.710
We've already run the numbers against
what's in the bureau's database,

14:05.710 --> 14:08.500
and made sure that there were
no clerical errors.

14:08.500 --> 14:10.330
You need to come with us now.

14:12.210 --> 14:14.710
Good grief, how depressing.

14:14.710 --> 14:18.000
It pains me to think that such a
dimwitted thug was serving among

14:18.000 --> 14:19.960
the Kingdom's nine cabinet ministers.

14:19.960 --> 14:22.500
And you had the nerve to call me greedy?

14:22.500 --> 14:25.830
You're the last person
I want to hear that from, Grimms!

14:25.830 --> 14:27.960
Hope you're ready to suffer.

14:28.210 --> 14:30.920
And be thankful embezzlement
is the only crime you're facing.

14:30.920 --> 14:32.630
Hah-hah!

14:36.580 --> 14:38.630
So tell me, Freddy.

14:38.630 --> 14:40.540
Are you the one behind this...?

14:40.540 --> 14:43.250
No clue. It's totally beyond me.

14:50.790 --> 14:53.210
Damn. They got me good.

14:53.210 --> 14:56.290
Never expected that I'd be making
such a bland exit.

14:56.750 --> 15:00.000
But you know what, Freddy?
I'm happy for you.

15:00.000 --> 15:03.170
Since neither you or any of your pals
died in the end.

15:03.580 --> 15:06.750
And everybody's celebrating the fact
we avoided a full-scale war.

15:06.750 --> 15:09.830
I mean, why wouldn't they?
War is just awful.

15:10.290 --> 15:11.630
That's true.

15:11.630 --> 15:13.960
I'm pretty sure the only people who want war...

15:13.960 --> 15:15.460
are greedy scumbags like you,

15:15.460 --> 15:18.920
who constantly prey on others by
taking advantage of their misfortune.

15:18.920 --> 15:20.960
What can I say?

15:21.330 --> 15:24.170
There will always be humans
who stand to gain from war.

15:24.790 --> 15:27.210
But if you wanna get specific...

15:27.210 --> 15:30.170
that applies to more than
just humans, ya know?

15:34.250 --> 15:37.710
Anyways, all this gossip
isn't really that important.

15:38.080 --> 15:39.790
What actually bums me out, Freddy...

15:40.580 --> 15:43.540
was that I never had the chance
to make you a real man.

15:43.540 --> 15:47.290
Because right now you're nothing but
a wishy-washy loser,

15:47.290 --> 15:50.540
tied down by stupid bullshit
like friendship and the past.

15:50.880 --> 15:52.290
Farewell, ladies and gents!

15:52.290 --> 15:53.630
Take care now!

15:59.460 --> 16:01.290
That's the end of that.

16:01.290 --> 16:04.630
Dark rumors about Grimms
have been around since forever.

16:04.630 --> 16:06.130
It's high time he paid the piper.

16:06.130 --> 16:08.580
Well, I wasn't told anything about this!

16:08.580 --> 16:12.290
You're such an honest person that we
figured it would show through if you knew.

16:12.290 --> 16:14.960
My sincere apologies for leaving you out.

16:14.960 --> 16:17.000
I would like an explanation as well.

16:17.000 --> 16:19.210
Why put on this farce?

16:19.210 --> 16:20.880
Do you all believe that Minister Grimms

16:20.880 --> 16:23.210
had something to do with the explosion
at the Magic Bureau?

16:23.210 --> 16:24.960
What are you talking about?

16:24.960 --> 16:27.040
I clearly stated that was an accident.

16:27.040 --> 16:28.170
Unless you're saying...

16:28.170 --> 16:32.210
that you know of something that can
definitively tie Grimm to it?

16:33.210 --> 16:35.040
No, let's just drop it.

16:35.290 --> 16:37.460
I actually owe him for helping me out.

16:37.460 --> 16:38.630
It's a shame what happened.

16:38.880 --> 16:41.460
But aren't you the person responsible for

16:41.460 --> 16:44.830
leaking the data that proved Grimms
was embezzling funds?

16:44.830 --> 16:46.330
I tip my hat to you for that one.

16:46.330 --> 16:48.540
No, I had nothing to do with it.

16:49.000 --> 16:50.000
Ah!

16:52.630 --> 16:53.830
What is it?

16:53.830 --> 16:55.290
Sorry, it's nothing!

16:56.540 --> 16:58.630
I just remembered something funny!

16:58.630 --> 17:00.250
His laugh creeps me out.

17:00.250 --> 17:01.290
Shhh!

17:01.540 --> 17:05.080
So, I played along with your
little farce as you asked.

17:05.080 --> 17:09.000
Now you're going to return the favor
by listening to my request, right?

17:09.000 --> 17:10.790
Yes, of course.

17:11.130 --> 17:13.630
That was always my intention.

17:14.040 --> 17:15.210
Fred, my boy.

17:15.210 --> 17:19.040
We're in a bit of a pickle with
an open spot on the board.

17:19.040 --> 17:22.210
After helping to end the war
with the demons ten years ago,

17:22.210 --> 17:24.580
you've saved the Kingdom once again.

17:24.580 --> 17:27.790
You're a perfect fit to take over
in the position of minister.

17:28.630 --> 17:31.500
Although Gelmof might blow a fuse
once he finds out.

17:40.250 --> 17:42.830
Well then, if that's the case...

17:45.710 --> 17:48.920
Holy crap, the Hero's groveling video
has over 10 million views now!

17:48.920 --> 17:50.540
That's hysterical!

17:51.000 --> 17:52.040
Jeez.

17:52.040 --> 17:54.380
I knew I shouldn't have done that...

17:54.710 --> 17:57.670
Totally ruins the mood for my
booze in the park time.

17:57.670 --> 17:59.790
And it was the one thing
I had to look forward to!

18:01.290 --> 18:03.420
Hello, Mr. Max! I'm a reporter
with Free Day Magazine!

18:03.420 --> 18:04.460
I'm with the Daily High Tide!

18:04.460 --> 18:05.750
I'm with Women Themselves!
I'm with Weekly Spring Equinox!<b></b>

18:05.920 --> 18:08.380
I gotta say, you really knocked it
out of the park the other day!

18:08.380 --> 18:11.210
Practically the entire Kingdom
has been lauding your actions!

18:11.210 --> 18:12.630
Tell us how it felt while you were groveling!

18:12.630 --> 18:16.420
Can you share the reasons behind your decision
to not side with either Fred or Leo?

18:16.420 --> 18:19.880
I understand that you're currently unemployed,
but do you have any plans for the future?

18:20.000 --> 18:21.380
SHADDUP!

18:21.380 --> 18:22.710
I'm a busy guy!

18:22.710 --> 18:24.750
Don't shove those friggin' cameras in my face!

18:25.710 --> 18:27.420
He flew away! Just look at the Hero go!

18:27.420 --> 18:28.420
Film him, film him!

18:28.420 --> 18:29.880
Stay on his tail!

18:30.580 --> 18:33.080
Aw jeez. What an awful ruckus.

18:33.080 --> 18:36.080
But whatever, it's still peaceful
on the whole around here.

18:36.380 --> 18:37.380
Yuria.

18:38.000 --> 18:39.290
Want to take a break?

18:39.290 --> 18:40.460
I'll look after the baby.

18:40.460 --> 18:41.630
Oh yeah?

18:41.630 --> 18:42.960
I guess I'll take you up on that.

18:42.960 --> 18:44.540
Max Serve!

18:44.750 --> 18:45.750
Too easy.

18:50.630 --> 18:52.080
I'm back...

18:52.330 --> 18:56.040
Friggin' hell. Those jerks made me
use up all my energy...

18:56.040 --> 18:57.830
Welcome back, Max!

18:57.830 --> 19:00.290
Looks like you successfully escaped
from all the paparazzi.

19:00.290 --> 19:02.290
Huh? How did you know that?

19:02.290 --> 19:04.080
We were watching it on TV the entire time.

19:04.080 --> 19:05.250
You gotta be kidding...

19:05.380 --> 19:09.040
Well, I guess since Max is all pooped out,
then tonight's dinner should be

19:09.040 --> 19:12.040
my stamina-boosting bowl
that's been all the rage lately!

19:12.040 --> 19:13.380
That sounds wonderful!

19:13.380 --> 19:15.960
Cool, I'll take mine with extra garlic...
no, wait.

19:15.960 --> 19:17.830
How long are you two gonna cramp my style?!

19:17.830 --> 19:20.580
I mean, it makes absolutely no sense
whatsoever for you to live here

19:20.580 --> 19:22.080
when we're mortal friggin' enemies!

19:22.080 --> 19:23.330
So get the hell out!

19:23.330 --> 19:25.710
All the problems with the Republic
have been resolved now!

19:25.710 --> 19:27.330
And I'm back in the Hero groove!

19:27.330 --> 19:28.540
That's a load of crap!

19:28.540 --> 19:30.290
You fought for like all of five minutes!

19:30.290 --> 19:32.960
That doesn't count as you
making a comeback as a Hero!

19:32.960 --> 19:35.830
You're still a long ways from returning to
what you were like in the glory days!

19:35.830 --> 19:38.290
Which means that I still have to
take care of you!

19:38.290 --> 19:40.170
HOW DOES THAT MAKE ANY
GODDAMN SENSE?!

19:40.170 --> 19:43.750
If that's what His Grace desires,
then I shall be staying as well.

19:44.000 --> 19:46.460
As his secretary, I am obliged to
keep him safe at all times.

19:46.460 --> 19:48.040
I'm not gonna lay a finger on him!

19:48.040 --> 19:49.500
Just get out of here right now!

19:49.500 --> 19:50.880
This is MY room!

19:50.880 --> 19:53.670
Oh? Are you sure you're
all right with that, Max?

19:53.670 --> 19:55.630
You'll never be able to eat my cooking again.

19:55.630 --> 19:57.500
Including my masterpiece,
the stamina-boosting bowl!

19:58.580 --> 19:59.630
And that's not all.

19:59.630 --> 20:02.750
There's my hamburg steak,
pizza, and even cake!

20:05.170 --> 20:07.040
You could at least make it
one last time before you leave.

20:07.040 --> 20:08.170
You said that you would, yeah?

20:08.500 --> 20:11.500
My tummy is already expecting to be fed
some of that stamina-boosting goodness!

20:12.500 --> 20:14.420
Guess you still can't beat your stomach, huh?

20:14.420 --> 20:16.500
Tsk. Leave already.

20:16.960 --> 20:19.380
Okay then, a toast to renewed friendships!

20:19.380 --> 20:21.630
Aw hell no!
I ain't drinking with you EVER again!

20:21.630 --> 20:22.880
Have no fear!

20:22.880 --> 20:25.580
For I never repeat the same mistake twice!

20:25.580 --> 20:27.460
Nope! No friggin' way!

20:27.460 --> 20:29.710
Come on. Just cut her some slack, Hero.

20:29.710 --> 20:31.960
Everybody makes mistakes, am I right?

20:32.330 --> 20:35.380
Let's see here.
"Max the Hero" and "scandal"...

20:35.380 --> 20:38.210
STOP IT! DON'T YOU DARE!

20:40.420 --> 20:42.210
Okay, here we go!

20:43.080 --> 20:45.830
Sorry, can we take one more?
I had my eyes closed again.

20:45.830 --> 20:48.630
Again?! Get a grip already, Leo!

20:48.630 --> 20:50.210
My bad.

20:50.210 --> 20:54.130
Well, to be fair, I wasn't really
feeling that last one myself.

20:58.670 --> 21:00.130
Okay! I'm all ready to go!

21:00.130 --> 21:01.330
Whoa, hold on!

21:01.330 --> 21:03.080
I'm gonna pose like this.

21:03.080 --> 21:04.580
Wait, no. Maybe this is better!

21:04.580 --> 21:05.670
Or actually...

21:06.580 --> 21:07.500
Like this?

21:07.500 --> 21:09.040
Or this!
Whatever, just get on with it!<b></b>

21:10.080 --> 21:11.790
Okay! Take it now!

21:11.790 --> 21:13.630
And... cheese!

21:20.250 --> 21:22.960
Guess that's the end of our heroic adventure.

21:23.330 --> 21:26.380
Well, there were a lot of challenges
we had to overcome.

21:26.880 --> 21:28.880
But everything worked out in the end.

21:31.710 --> 21:33.130
This is it.

21:33.130 --> 21:34.420
I won't be seeing you guys ever again.

21:34.420 --> 21:35.460
Huh?

21:38.630 --> 21:41.250
I mean, the world's gonna be at peace, right?

21:45.290 --> 21:46.830
Well, goodbye.

21:47.960 --> 21:50.790
Be careful and don't get attacked
on your way home, okay?

21:51.710 --> 21:53.790
Alright! See you on the flip side!

22:07.540 --> 22:11.000
<b>Level 1 Demon Lord</b>

22:07.540 --> 22:11.000
<b>and One Room Hero</b>
